WEBVTT

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:18.210
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.750
Flying through the mesh of clouds

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.290
Our dancing wings wrap up in the wind

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.750
Stars fall right before our eyes

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.040
The blue of all blues that drew us in

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.080
We kicked up off the blurring ground

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.290
Let me hear the sound of the sky you know

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:56.630
Take flight make gravity your ally

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:03.040
One more time, however many 
times, laughing all along

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:10.080
We would never look back when we fly

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.290
An everlasting dream we 
live in pursuit of tomorrow

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.790
Amid rising despair I locked away my love

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.080
I hate my weak self

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:27.040
Here and now passes by as 
we head towards the future

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.790
Yikes! I forgot Malo!

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:36.630
Do you honestly plan on 
taking that thing with you?

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:37.540
You really shouldn't!

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:38.810
I'm heading out ahead, then.

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.420
You can't wait for us?

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.210
What does it matter?
We're headed off to different places anyway.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.000
We could still stay together
at least as far as Shibushiku.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.380
Kate, I got us a map of 
the way out to Teikatsu.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.330
Understood.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.710
Kylie, the rest of us might 
be away for a while...

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.710
But don't you go tarnishing 
the Corps while we're gone.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:57.290
In other words, do behave yourself.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.420
Yeah yeah yeah yeah...

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:58.830
I've got those engines warmed and ready and

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.720
you're just gonna sit around 
taking your sweet time?!

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.000
Someone got the runs or something?

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.330
We're coming, we're coming.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.870
You hold down the fort 
while we're away, Kylie.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.540
The Hagoromo's in your hands now.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.700
Yep.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.180
Not like it's going anywhere
since it's grounded for repairs.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.670
If you want a souvenir I could
get you something, you know!

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:15.420
No thanks.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.290
Really now? Fine, you get nothing!

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:25.210
The Vagabond Spruce

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.790
What's with that sleepy face?

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.040
I'm just so bored.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.710
Everyone else sure seemed busy.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.380
They sure love to work, huh?

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:42.290
And here we were with a whole month off.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.080
I'd think almost anyone would jump at
the chance for work with a twenty percent raise.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.630
Not you?

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.420
I'd go if I could just fly 
wherever I want however I want.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.710
Well that wouldn't be work now, would it?

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.250
I always thought you loved the work you do.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:58.460
I mean, I don't hate it!

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.420
It's how I get to fly.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.670
I'll clean that up for you if 
you aren't going to finish it.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.420
What?! Not a chance!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.200
I thought so.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.410
What, you want me to tell you a story?

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.210
Mhmm.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.080
Well, when you put me 
on the spot like that...

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.460
Back during out transport 
of the fish to Ikesuka...

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.330
The brave KOTOBUKI Corps 
put on a fantastic show.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.180
Their popularity has since sky rocketed,

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:25.550
and the phones have rung off 
the hook to get 'em booked!

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.130
That's a boring story.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.670
Okay, then...

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:31.540
How about how the Ouni Company has
temporarily called off all operations?

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.110
All pilots are free to take on side jobs,
and they'll still get their normal salaries, too!

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.460
First Off, you're the 
most boring person ever.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:38.540
I get that a lot.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.880
Tanbabajin baranzura!

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.460
Ranzura!

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.330
What does that even mean?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.830
Hey! You're Reona's lackey!

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.880
I'm no lackey, I'm Kylie!

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.960
What are you doing out here, lackey-Kylie?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.040
Just getting some air.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.830
How, like this?

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.130
Like this?

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.420
No, I'm just walking around aimlessly.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.580
You don't even have anywhere to go?

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.250
Why not?

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:05.670
She told me she had no 
place to go before, too!

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.500
No, I didn't!

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.330
Yes, you did!

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.500
Check out those planes! Awesome!

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.710
There's so many!

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.290
Where are a bunch of planes 
like that headed for?

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.630
Know what? I thought up something I can do.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.630
Oh yeah, what?

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:20.030
I'm gonna steal you two away
and boil you up into a stew!

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.960
Bwahahaha!

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.080
Tanbabajin!

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.960
And here I was thinking we were going
to be on high alert. What a disappointment.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.580
They're just so happy to declare themselves
a sister city with Ikesuka now.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.380
So they've poured plenty of extra funds
into the ceremony.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.050
On this? Do they have brains 
in those heads of theirs?

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.000
You sure have developed 
quite the sharp tongue, hmm?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:52.250
Back at school you were much
more close-minded and stubborn.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.880
But now I hear they call you
"Emma the Fierce", was it?

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.580
What a wonderful nickname!

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.500
She who touches pitch shall 
be defiled therewith, yes?

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:04.750
People talk of our corps like 
we're a pack of racketeers.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.670
I've heard talk.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.170
And it would seem you are quite the pilot.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.410
Am I, though?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.790
I simply fly because it's the 
only way to earn a living.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.000
Well, I won't try and nose my way
in any deeper than that.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.710
Oh, but how is your family?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.960
Now, just as always, I am astounded that
they still think I am just merrily traveling the world.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.960
They even ask me to bring back souvenirs.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:26.760
Oh my...

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.970
But knowing you, I bet you do just that, yes?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.890
It's as if they think money just bubbles up from
below their feet, and it's really too much.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:40.420
I'm sure your whole family 
is so proud of you, though.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.770
Just the other day someone trying to pass themselves off


00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:47.050
as an old friend tried to 
borrow money from them.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.080
Oh my, not again?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.380
Even after they nearly lost 
everything in a scam before...

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.590
They're still managing 
to at least stay afloat,

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.080
so people must think they 
are sitting on some fortune.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.170
Did they really fall for it again?

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.630
I stopped them just moments 
before the deal was sealed.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.630
What a close call! You poor thing.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:07.250
Adversity makes a man wise, you know.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.040
I don't need them to be wise.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.670
I just wish they would cut 
back on the adversity.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.920
Well, perhaps it's time we get to work.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.080
We're meant to patrol the 
airspace above the venue, yes?

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.330
I never figured Nakamizu 
would be the sort to retire.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.830
I figured they were in this for life.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:31.460
With this whole new license system and
union registration and what not...

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:34.290
Apparently they just got fed 
up with all the red tape.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.620
Unions?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.040
Areshima has those, sure, but...

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.750
But... We've got them out here
in the middle of nowhere, too.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:45.460
Not just the fighter pilots either,
but postal workers like us, too.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.540
It's ridiculous, really.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.540
And it's only gotten worse since last month.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.510
I've never been good with paperwork either,
so it has been quite rough.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:54.580
Yeah, huh?

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.470
What has the world come to?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.460
I mean sure, that probably makes me
sound old and grouchy, but...

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.170
Listen to yourself.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.330
If you're old, what does that make me?

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.920
Don't you worry, you'll never be
a day over seventeen, Higako.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.460
And you're right with me, Musako!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:22.380
I asked to be put on the waiting list
a whole month ago! What's the deal!

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.380
I'm sorry, that particular 
book is just ever so popular.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.250
I heard it is at least being 
put back in print again, but...

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:29.960
I'm really sorry.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:31.510
There you are!

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.540
I knew the Shibushiku Library would have it!

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:36.330
"The Final Shopping Wave"

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.900
I finally got my hands on it!

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.210
Why's a book from Ikesuka so hot?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.670
You telling me all these people out here
are dying to learn more about the place?

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.670
Well, it is the greatest city in the land!

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.610
People just want to stay in the know.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:59.170
Why should a city like Gadoll, a place with
it's own culture, history, and environment...

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:05.420
have to adopt the nonsensical ways of a completely
unrelated city like Ikesuka and its mayor?

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:06.380
Get out of here!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:06.830
Traitor!

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.250
Half-wit!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.130
If we give up our autonomy, 
this city is done for!

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.220
How can you be so blind?!

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.500
Piss off!

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.580
Learn some sense!

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.930
Quit being so stuck in the past!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:19.220
Councilor Julia! I must ask you retract
your statements and apologize!

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.960
I have merely spoken the truth.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:21.710
I will not retract a word!

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:22.380
Get her out of here!

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:23.330
Wait just a minute.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:24.460
What about our vote?

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:27.750
Are we not here to vote on whether or not
we enter into the Brotherhood of Freedom Union?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.880
You have been ordered to leave. Begone!

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.630
You dare try and defy me of my right
as councilor to vote?!

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:34.580
Go on and get lost!

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:35.500
Get outta here!

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.290
Even life as an air pirate would be
better than working for Isao!

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.170
What was that?!

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:43.920
Enough of your nonsense!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:44.830
Get her off this council!

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.880
Bribes and collusion.
Embezzlement and voters right violations.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.460
Every last one of those senile old men
has dirty laundry to air out.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.220
And I think it's time for a laundry day.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.710
But Lady Julia...

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.880
You're right, it's the younger bunch
that are the real problem.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.880
They're the ones that fall for Isao and
his fake image without so much as a push.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:03.710
You don't have to dig far to see
how thoughtless they are.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:05.040
It's pathetic, honestly.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.920
That's not what I meant. I 
think you are in true danger.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:09.710
What?

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:11.880
You should flee this place.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:13.960
Are you serious?

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:14.460
I am...

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.920
I say this with one thousand 
percent certainty.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:30.790
Run for cover!

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:31.540
'kay!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.890
Now where'd you go?

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.040
Gotcha, Miyuri!

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:43.600
Liar!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.750
I'm not! You're behind the tree! I found you!

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.000
Too bad you'll never find a purpose in life.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.670
Well aren't you a clever one!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.210
Goodbye can!

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.420
Shoot!

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:59.270
You're the worst, Captain!

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:00.960
What's your deal?!

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.960
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:08.000
Do you want to hear what I have for you today,
or what I have for you tomorrow?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.630
I wanna hear whichever is better.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.710
Well, that all depends on you.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.720
I'll start with today.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:17.880
Allen wants to go out for a scenic flight
around Rahama, it seems.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:18.670
What?

00:10:18.670 --> 00:10:22.670
I'm sure he'd ask Kate if she were around,
but she's away in Doan.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:26.130
As for tomorrow, I've got an 
invitation to work elsewhere.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.380
What?! You're leaving the Ouni Company?

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:29.910
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.000
The invitation is for the KOTOBUKI Corps.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.540
The offer comes from a 
company out in Areshima.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:36.330
Why?!

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:37.130
Why indeed?

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.430
They say they'll offer you 
twice your current pay.

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:43.210
Seems it would make things easier if you
all took the offer, but they'll take even one of you.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:47.830
They say they'll look into getting you
whatever aircraft you want, too.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.210
The Tamsin Company?

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:51.500
I feel like I've heard 
that name before, maybe...

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.210
They're the biggest name in distribution.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.920
They just announced they'll be teaming up
with View Trading the other day.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.840
That's Isao's place! No way!

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:02.580
The offer is open until the end of the month.
Why don't you think it over?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.170
But...!

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:03.600
What?

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.000
Are you trying to say you 
don't need us anymore?

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.670
I have no right to order you to stay.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:16.330
And don't come expecting me
to drop down and beg you, either.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.130
You can make this choice yourself.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.580
It sounds like a great chance.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.750
Do you seriously think so?

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:26.130
I'd at least be a little tempted.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:27.080
You're awful.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.750
I mean, flying is flying, right?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.130
We all need money, too.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:37.090
Can you at least quit drinking 
while we're up here?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.000
Why?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.290
'Cause I said so!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.580
Oh, fine then.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:41.430
Sorry.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.830
It's not like I've got time 
to waste with you out here.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:46.970
I'm super busy with all my can-kicking
and soul searching.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:50.790
Say Thunderbolt, do you remember
when the hole closed up?

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.380
Quit calling me that.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.750
It was seventy years ago.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:54.330
Nope!

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:54.830
What?!

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:58.580
There's reason to believe it has opened
and closed again since then.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.670
Yeah, right!

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.460
Did you see it? You didn't, did you?

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:02.280
I guess not.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.530
Because I was shot down by 
some unidentified planes,

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.010
just before I found the proof I needed.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:12.920
And I've been stuck in a wheel chair,
never making it up above 60 centi-khrill since.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.500
Sure, these were probably smaller holes.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:21.870
Nothing of the scale of the one
that brought the Yufang here.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.250
But if they did in fact open...

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:25.680
Then what?

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:29.890
Someone may have made there way here and
done whatever it is they came to do.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.460
What? What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.640
Or maybe they did nothing at all.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:34.500
That's a big difference!

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:36.290
Mind if I take just one sip?

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:37.150
Not a chance!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:41.170
You're so cruel, Thunderbolt. 
This is the only fun I get.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:44.920
Yeah right! You have plenty
of fun talking about that hole.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:47.080
You noticed?

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:51.290
Excuse me...

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:56.470
No need to get all worked up, I'm 
just here for a little visit.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:58.170
Hideaki, sir! This way!

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.670
Yes, yes, I'll be right there.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.590
So you just keep quiet, yes?

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.930
If you don't, well...

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:08.380
Sir, look.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:10.790
My, well what have we here?

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:14.580
This won't do. Drinking while 
crippled is just inexcusable.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:15.790
We'll be relieving him of this.

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:17.630
What about this?

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:19.540
This is...

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:24.040
Oh, even worse. We'll 
definitely be taking this.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:27.630
It's the owner himself who I 
think is due to be tossed out!

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.880
Can you bank at a forty five degree angle and
turn us around one full rotation to the right?

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:33.000
What? Why?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.040
Just something I want to check.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.210
Fine, I guess...

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.950
What are you doing back there?

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:50.330
What would you do if you had
the chance to go to Yufang?

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.380
What?

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.750
I guess I'd look for Ol' Sab.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:54.750
Ol' who?

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:55.880
A friend of yours?

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.120
More like my grandpa.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.790
I mean, not literally, but he 
was just this normal old guy.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:03.040
Maybe not all that normal, though.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.170
What do you mean?

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:07.530
When I was a kid he took me up in his plane,


00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.470
but then he just vanished, 
and I never saw him again.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.080
What does that have to do with Yufang?

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.580
Can't say for sure, but he 
might have been from Yufang.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.880
He had tons of Yufang 
stuff. Books, even planes.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:20.580
He had a Hayabusa?

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:23.770
No, he had a Zero. A model 32!

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:27.290
I thought I was gonna pee myself
the first time he took me for a ride!

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:28.300
It was amazing!

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.390
Jumping back to that new job offer,
they might have model 32s too, you know.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.080
What?

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:36.130
What would you do if you had the chance
to fly in one again?

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:39.040
I wouldn't care. The 
Hayabusa is still the best.

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.770
And the only real 32 was Ol' Sab's!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.250
All others are fakes! I hate 'em!
I wish they'd all just blow up!

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.580
Am I sensing a grudge?

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:46.420
Nope!

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.000
Well, maybe.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:47.920
Really, now?

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.210
Can you take us up to a thousand khrill?

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:52.450
'spose so.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.380
Turn us right and upwards at 
a five hundred khrill radius.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:56.330
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.880
Hold altitude here and turn us left.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:01.880
Yep, yep, yep.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.580
Now let's zoom up to fifteen hundred.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.080
Aka-tombo can't fly that high!

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:16.220
Wait...

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:21.330
There!

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:21.790
What?!

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.500
Cut it and stop here.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.920
Not a chance!

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:27.710
What... is that?

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.670
Uh, hello?

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:32.630
Huh? Oh.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:34.330
Is that... the hole?

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.290
No, it's not open now.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:39.040
It's probably just going to disappear.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.330
Is there a chance it might open?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:40.960
There is.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:41.960
That's incredi-

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:44.880
Who-what-why?!

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.790
Maybe I was a little too focused on
my calculations and observations.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:50.040
You think?!

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.630
Uh-oh. Are those Shiden-kai?

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:07.330
Those aren't the sorts you want to face in
this under powered Type 95 Intermediate Trainer.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.000
Well, that's an understatement!

00:16:09.670 --> 00:16:13.830
Still, they sure don't seem 
ready to go easy on us.

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:16.420
It's been so long since 
I've been in a dogfight!

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.710
This is so exciting!

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:18.960
Are you crazy?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.960
It's not even a "fight" if we don't have
any means of fighting back!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.630
Just like you wouldn't call an army chasing
down an unarmed civilian a war!

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.750
True!

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:27.210
Huh?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.630
I've got a little favor to ask.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.260
What?

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:34.130
See, I've got much better aim 
with a little drink in me.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:35.510
Whaddya say?

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.250
If you're lying, you're really in for it.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:37.970
I'd never!

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:45.210
Tell me Thunderbolt, what sort of flaws
do you think those birds have?

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.790
Uhh... they're too heavy?

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:48.040
There's that.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:51.040
But even more than that, 
they're just too fast.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:51.750
What?!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:54.480
Plus, they aren't built for turns.

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:57.210
They have to take these big, long arcs.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:03.710
This 95 might be slow, under-armed, and paper-thin,
but we can use that all to our advantage.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:24.960
They're coming straight at us!

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:27.710
We're sitting ducks if they 
come at us that way, huh.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.330
Thunderbolt, point us down.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:33.040
Uh-huh!

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:55.470
They're in my blind spot!

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:56.380
Can you roll right?

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:56.930
C'mon!

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:14.920
What the heck?!

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.750
What are we gonna do?!

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:22.960
Steady now, steady.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:12.170
You think I'm going down? Not a chance!
Not in your wildest dreams!

00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:48.790
You're pretty good at 
faking dead, Thunderbolt!

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.000
Not that I ever wanted to be!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.380
Don't let your pride get the better of you!

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.250
Just shrug it off, shrug it off!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.040
This is clearly Ikesuka 
meddling in our affairs!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.340
Whatever do you mean?

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.050
We here have a commitment
to protect the people of Ikesuka.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:06.930
If you do not hold up your end of the deal,

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:10.270
we'll be forced to see you as 
cohorts with those awful pirates.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:16.750
It's unfortunate that it has come to this,
but we will now be bombing your capitol building.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.500
I never would have...

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:29.620
I've already talked with Kylie,
but I want you to tell the others.

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.330
What's your stance, Madame?

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:36.540
I have none. I don't plan on 
meddling in your decision.

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:38.880
Things will go as they go.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.590
It's pointless trying to force 
others to do as you wish.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:44.830
Not impossible, but "pointless?"

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:45.790
Oh, yes.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:48.970
What would you consider 
as having a "point," then?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:51.890
The freedom to choose.

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:53.420
Interesting...

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:56.630
You sure do love getting shot down, doncha?

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.290
Probably even more than you like
shooting other people down, huh?

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:00.330
Chika, watch your mouth!

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:03.400
This was more of an accident 
than anything else.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.630
Yeah, ok?

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:07.790
And you, show some more appreciation
to Chika for coming out to save you!

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.330
What?!

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:13.040
Thank you so very much, Chika.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.500
I am simply glad you are all right.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.210
Thank you, thank you, and thank you.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:18.790
Oh, nonsense.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.330
Oh, yeah! Madame!

00:21:21.330 --> 00:21:23.340
I'm not leaving the Corps!

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:24.880
Is that so?

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:28.210
I don't wanna take orders from or
have to listen to anyone but Reona.

00:21:28.210 --> 00:21:31.460
Plus, another hole might 
open up over Rahama soon!

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:32.930
I don't wanna miss that!

00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:33.960
What?!

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:38.380
A hole? Surrender? Invasion? Alliance?

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:42.000
How am I supposed to follow
if you just keep going on and on?

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.580
Trim it down for me.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:46.290
To put it simply, things are heating up,
and going swimmingly.

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:47.790
That is all.

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:48.790
Oh, okay!

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:50.960
Swimmingly, huh?

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:54.500
Quite swimmingly, I dare say.

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:08.580
I wanted to try and soar through that sky

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:12.420
So I wished upon the winds right before me

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:16.330
Our aspirations build us scenery

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.750
I wonder how that wind is now

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:29.080
Why do we fight, I wonder

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:33.130
What is our purpose here?

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:41.380
I asked, but the skies do not answer

00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:49.040
We all have wings

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:53.750
Far away at the end of all lament

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:58.000
The stories we found

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:05.750
No one can steal these skies away

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:10.460
We will soar unafraid of anything

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:17.630
Because happiness is right here

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:27.500
Preview

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:37.710
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"The Aggressive Bombers"!

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:41.000
The Aggressive Bombers
